#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The coordinator assigns the translation to a qualified translator, ideally a domain SME for the content area. For WHO content, the translator should be familiar with WHO SMART Guidelines terminology. The assignment includes: - The .pot file(s) from extraction - The domain glossary - Context notes (block kind, chapter, content area) - The deadline"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The coordinator selects: - Which content nodes need translation (block, section, chapter, or folio) - The target locale (one of the supportedLocales in harness.config.json) - The priority and deadline"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:187
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer annotates specific passages that need correction and returns to the translator with detailed feedback. Each annotation includes: - The passage in question - What is wrong (terminology, meaning, style) - The suggested correction or reference"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:200
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer signs off the translation, making it official. This records: - signedOffBy: the reviewer's identity - signedOffAt: the current timestamp - sourceHash: SHA-256 of the source .md - level: block | section | chapter | folio Tool: translation_signoff MCP tool"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:121
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The translator receives: - .pot file with source strings (msgid) - Domain glossary with approved term translations - Context notes per string - Style guide and WHO terminology references Tools: Poedit, Weblate, Crowdin, or direct .po editing."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:148
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The translator submits the completed .po file back to the pipeline. This may happen via: - Git commit + push - Weblate/Crowdin sync - File upload to the coordinator"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:136
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The translator works through each msgid, producing msgstr translations. They: - Follow the domain glossary for technical terms - Preserve placeholder tokens ({1}, {2}) in position - Mark uncertain translations as #fuzzy - Note any source ambiguities for the coordinator"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/human-translation-workflow.bpmn:135
#. Diagram label
msgid "Translate strings in preferred tool"
msgstr ""

